  "notes": "Fire Tester 0.1.754b\n\nSince 0.1.753b, this release adds an optional immutable PSRAM Smoke render cache with a pixel-equivalent fallback and request-scoped first running cooler-stale diagnostics. Cadence, quality, brightness, thresholds, output arbitration and safety limits are unchanged. BatteryHealth, SOC and persistence behavior are unchanged.\n\nThirty-five host suites passed with the same 1,439 production inputs used for the checked build. The 3,176,992-byte normal image was installed: 776 blocks and full END acknowledged in 77.79 s. Fresh normal 754 identity and idle outputs were verified after one supported post-update restart. The initial post-update identity attempt received no response; a separate retry succeeded.\n\nCold cartridge identification passed with four early and three late samples, 0.8738 ohm. Readback showed present, unblocked, 874 milliohm, quality 60%, and zero faults. Fresh UI1 checks passed cartridge presence/quality, heater NTC 23.074 C, primary IR 82 mm and cartridge IR 59 mm. Cleanup left idle Desktop with outputs, lease and radio pause at zero. The 64-record learning dataset is unchanged, generation 90/revision 31.\n\nSixteen settled Desktop samples had median start-to-start period 17,102.5 us, inverse-period estimate 58.4711 FPS and work 14,155.5 us. Earlier 753 samples measured 18,787 us, 53.2502 FPS and 17,051 us. These sequential unpaired observations show a shorter observed period, not a controlled causal benchmark or sustained 60 FPS. Cache allocation was not independently visible in the captured log.\n\nCooler request 3 failed in running site 3: charger-current telemetry unavailable while both INA readings and attachment state were fresh. Five qualified loaded samples averaged 702.1 mA. This narrows the generic INA_STALE report; the producer failure branch and fan health remain unproven. No thresholds were widened. Full QA, physical controls/phone BLE validation, independent AI calibration and a hosted QR/help URL remain open.\n",
